@startuml UC-24 Edit Own Blog Post - Sequence Diagram (stereo)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280

actor "Teacher or Moderator" as User
participant ":BlogCommunityPage" as UI <<user interaction>>
participant ":CreatePostModal" as EDITOR <<user interaction>>
participant ":BlogController" as CTL <<coordinator>>
participant ":BlogPostService" as SVC <<business logic>>
participant ":BlogPostRepository" as POSTS <<interface>>
database DB

autonumber
activate User
User ->> UI : Open the three-dot menu of an own post and select "Edit"
activate UI
UI ->> UI : openEdit(id)
UI ->> EDITOR : Open the Blog Editor with the current title, body, subject tag and cover
activate EDITOR
User ->> EDITOR : Change the title, body or subject tag

opt user cancels the editing
  User ->> EDITOR : Close the Blog Editor
  EDITOR -->> User : Close the editor and leave the published post unchanged
end

User ->> EDITOR : Click "Save"
EDITOR ->> EDITOR : handleSubmit()
EDITOR ->> CTL : PATCH /api/blog-posts/{id}
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : update(id, title, content, subject, thumbnailUrl)
activate SVC
SVC ->> POSTS : findPublishedById(id)
activate POSTS
POSTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM blog_posts WHERE id = ? AND status = 'PUBLISHED'
activate DB
DB -->> POSTS : row / none
deactivate DB
POSTS -->> SVC : BlogPost
deactivate POSTS
SVC ->> SVC : check that the signed-in user is the author, keep the untouched fields and sanitize the new body HTML

alt the post is unavailable, the user is not the author, a required field is empty or saving fails
  SVC -->> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException / ForbiddenOperationException / IllegalArgumentException
  CTL -->> EDITOR : HTTP 404 / 403 / 400
  EDITOR -->> User : Show MSG02, MSG25 or the not-permitted message and keep the edits in the Blog Editor

else the author saves valid content
  SVC ->> POSTS : save(updated post)
  activate POSTS
  POSTS ->> DB : UPDATE blog_posts SET the edited fields and updated_at WHERE id = ?
  activate DB
  DB -->> POSTS : Saved
  deactivate DB
  POSTS -->> SVC : BlogPost
  deactivate POSTS
  SVC -->> CTL : BlogPostDetail
  CTL -->> EDITOR : HTTP 200 + BlogPostDetail
  EDITOR ->> UI : Hand the saved post back and close the Blog Editor
  deactivate EDITOR
  UI -->> User : Show MSG08 and display the updated blog post
end
deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
deactivate User
@enduml
